  "bootstrapRegistryHazards20261027": {
    "sourceBase": "1b5db62227d092ebe1a2b7b3bb5c6aac0c95f4f4",
    "scope": "Full readable bootstrap5, registry4(including previously read unregister) and hazards4 bodies. Settings/default registration bodies, maintenance, group release descendants and other feature callers remain unread.",
    "findings": [
      "Bootstrap starts on server and noninterface machines. Discovery appends allUnits and registers only eligible local units; this is periodic discovery, not a strictly event-only registry. Actor Local handlers queue gain/unregister loss; new local registration resets local state to idle rather than proving continuation of the old task.",
      "Stop removes mission handlers, sound FiredMan handlers, global hazard/report arrays and unregisters managed units. The6 per-unit reaction/locality handlers are retained under a per-machine handlersOwner guard, not removed by unregister/stop. Most reactions guard registered/local state; dependent group release helpers still need their own ownership/body review. No claim that stop is an all-writer quiescence acknowledgement.",
      "Suppressed/Hit store live attacker getPosATL rather than a sensed belief; do not import as hidden enemy contact evidence. Native AmmoExplodedNear records actual local blast position with a short age bound.",
      "Hazard registration caches grenade/shell class facts, requires a positive timeToExplosion, caps registry128 and checks nearby projectile sight before a delayed reaction. Skill/suppression/injury affect latency. This is useful perception/fuse intent; getShotInfo index2 confirmed against official command documentation, not effective projectile lifetime.",
      "Evasion uses9 bounded candidate headings, reserved squad endpoints, increased hazard distance, water/slope/occupancy checks and sparse path/screening rays. It resets candidate height toground and uses linear projectile prediction capped0.6s without collision/gravity; do not claim native indoor/ballistic-path accuracy.",
      "React forces MOVE/TARGET/AUTOTARGET/posture/speed changes after state admission. updateHazardState can issue STOP/posture before the general updateState performs mission-order/timeout checks. CBE retains original actor/task authority instead of importing this extra writer."
    ],
    "commandReference": "https://community.bistudio.com/wiki/getShotInfo",
    "selectedContribution": "Avoid giving multiple immediate-hazard responders the same cover/escape destination; retain CBE single-grenade finite job and existing actor reservation/cleanup rather than source global per-actor hazard loop.",
    "remaining": "Predictive visible fuse-aware hazard selection, obstacle/floor-aware escape, legitimate emergency interruption and full feature-caller/cleanup reconciliation remain separate gaps; no whole source parity."
  },
  "grenadeEndpointSeparationImplementation20261027": {
    "sourceIntent": "Source findEvasionPosition rejects points already reserved for hazard responders. Adapt that intent inside the existing CBE event job, without copying source code or replacing state ownership.",
    "defect": "CortexGrenadeCheck passed[] reserved positions into every FindCover call, despite retaining issued destinations in regroupActors. FindCover could repeatedly select one post and its unscreened seed fallback bypassed reservation checks.",
    "change": "Pass issued job endpoints into existing FindCover. Test returned point, original away seed and2 nearby away bearings against already-issued endpoints (2m horizontal spacing) and increased distance from observed grenade. Reject before support PATH hold mutation when no candidate qualifies. Preserve exact six-second actor lease, native clearance-return proposal and existing delayed regroup/ownership policy.",
    "limits": "Endpoint separation within one local grenade job only; not actor-body/path clearance, collision avoidance, cross-grenade reservations, guaranteed blast cover, projectile-motion prediction or successful physical escape. No terrain-only selector added to misrepresent indoor floors/bridges as ground routing.",
    "expectedCost": "Existing16-actor bound and one cover search per eligible reacting actor retained. Up to4 fallback candidates against at most15 previously issued points; extra reserved-distance checks in the existing bounded cover search. No additional world query, worker, timer, setting or global state. Actual cost unmeasured.",
